# Copy to .env.local for local overrides. Real values are set in the host's
# build environment (Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables).

# Canonical public origin. Drives robots.txt / sitemap.xml (scripts/generate-seo-files.mjs)
# and the og:url / og:image share tags (vite.config.ts). No trailing slash.
# Build-time only, NOT prefixed with VITE_ — it never reaches the browser bundle.
SITE_URL=https://thaidongdee.com

# GA4 measurement ID. Leave EMPTY everywhere except production: when it is unset,
# no GA script is loaded and no events are sent (see src/analytics/ga.ts).
VITE_GA_ID=

# Canonical public origin for the BROWSER bundle. Used for auth e-mail links
# (sign-up confirmation, password reset) so a sign-up started on a local dev
# server still points people at the real site, not http://localhost. No trailing
# slash. In production the running origin already is the real site, so this is
# only strictly needed for local testing. Must also be on Supabase's redirect
# allow-list (Auth → URL Configuration). Set this to the deployed URL, e.g.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://thaidongdee.com
VITE_SITE_URL=

# Supabase (browser). The anon key is public by design — RLS decides everything.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# SERVER / CLI ONLY — never prefix with VITE_, never commit, never put in the
# browser: the service_role key bypasses RLS. Used by
# scripts/upload-catalog-images.mjs and scripts/import-project.mjs to write into
# the "catalog" Storage bucket.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# The admin user-management endpoint (functions/api/admin-users.ts, a Cloudflare
# Pages Function) also needs SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — set it as a PRODUCTION
# secret in Cloudflare Pages → project → Settings → Environment variables (NOT
# here, and NOT with a VITE_ prefix). The function reuses VITE_SUPABASE_URL /
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY already configured there. Until it is set, /admin/users
# still shows the list and role changes still work; invite / change-email /
# reset-password / rename are disabled with an in-page notice.
#
# The GA4 stats endpoint (functions/api/ga-stats.ts, a Cloudflare Pages Function)
# reads visitor numbers for the /admin dashboard with a Google SERVICE ACCOUNT,
# whose key must never reach the browser. Set these three as PRODUCTION env vars
# in Cloudflare Pages (GA_SA_PRIVATE_KEY as a SECRET; none use a VITE_ prefix).
# The service account must also be granted Viewer on the GA4 property. Until all
# three are set, the dashboard GA card shows its empty structure with a note.
# Putting the same three in `.env.local` ALSO lights up the card under
# `pnpm run dev` (vite-dev-api.mts mirrors the endpoint locally) — the private
# key as a single line with \n, in quotes, exactly as pasted into Cloudflare.
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=          # numeric property id (e.g. 557855535), NOT the G-… id
# GA_SA_CLIENT_EMAIL=       # e.g. ga-reader@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# GA_SA_PRIVATE_KEY=        # the service account's private key ("-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n…")
#
# Contact-message notifier (functions/api/notify-contact.ts, a Cloudflare Pages
# Function). A Supabase Database Webhook on contact_messages (INSERT) POSTs each
# new message here, and it e-mails the team (Brevo) and pushes LINE. Set these as
# PRODUCTION env vars in Cloudflare Pages (the key/token as SECRETS; no VITE_
# prefix). Each channel is independent — leave a channel's vars unset to skip it.
# Then create the webhook: Supabase → Database → Webhooks → table
# contact_messages, event Insert, HTTP Request, URL
# https://thaidongdee.com/api/notify-contact, header
# "x-webhook-secret: <CONTACT_WEBHOOK_SECRET>".
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=   # a random string; also the webhook's x-webhook-secret header
# BREVO_API_KEY=            # Brevo v3 API key (SECRET)
# NOTIFY_EMAIL_TO=          # e.g. contact@thaidongdee.com
# NOTIFY_EMAIL_FROM=        # a Brevo-verified sender address
# NOTIFY_EMAIL_FROM_NAME=   # optional sender display name
# LINE_CHANNEL_ACCESS_TOKEN=  # Messaging API long-lived channel access token (SECRET)
# LINE_NOTIFY_TO=           # push target(s): staff group/room/user id(s), comma-separated (REQUIRED for LINE)
